recommendation.text:
Untrusted data should never be used in a Java Naming and Directory Interface (JNDI) lookup. If your application requires dynamic JNDI lookups, then restrict those lookups to a known set of safe values using a validator function.

// DynamicJNDILookup.java
void validateName(String name) {
  if (!allowedNames.contains(name)) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException(name + " is not an allowed name for JNDI lookups");
  }
}

// DynamicJNDILookup.java
String name = request.getParameter("name");
Context context = new InitialContext();
validateName(name);
Object result = context.lookup(name);

Assess users should take care to add a validator such as validateName as a Security Control, to make Assess aware that this custom code validates that lookups are safe from JNDI injection vulnerabilities.

